From 739159fa2f32591728accc3c138a22664096f24a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:39:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: sound output through Web Audio

- WasmSound: the fake driver's paced Sound Manager mix goes to the page.
- The old Sound Driver (refNum -4): free-form writes play through a
  private Sound Manager channel; Control calls succeed; KillIO stops it.
- Programs that write samples straight into the buffer at SoundBase
  (Dark Castle, Glider 4) are sampled once per VBL.
- Fix the inverted --nosound switch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
